WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:02.936
-President Trump has fired

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.204
Secretary of State
Rex Tillerson,

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:06.606
which brings us to a segment
we call "Couple Things."

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.178 line:0%
-First thing...

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.879
Tillerson found out
that he was fired

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:15.348
from a Trump tweet.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:18.718
Even when you get fired from
Dominoes, the manager takes you

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:22.021
into that crappy little office
and tells you to your face.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:24.557
Tweets are for finding out
which band is in town

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:28.327
or which airline was mean
to Chrissy Teigen.

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:30.563
And, of course, Trump didn't
fire Tillerson to his face,

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.565
just like he didn't fire
James Comey to his face.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.634
Basically, if you're
over 6 feet tall,

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:37.971
Trump wants no part
of giving you bad news.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:41.140
That's why he's jumping at the
chance to meet with Kim Jong Un.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.145
"He's how short? Oh, I'll look
like a giant next to him."

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:50.049 line:0%
Second thing...

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:52.685
I'm not saying Rex Tillerson
was a great Secretary of State.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.521
He had the energy
of a 14-year-old bloodhound

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:58.224
on his third mint julep.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:02.128
He always looked like he was
walking through a fart cloud.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.930
But if you're gonna fire
competent secretaries

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.031
for being bad at their jobs,

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:06.833
let me refer you
to Betsy DeVos' appearance

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.268
on "60 Minutes."

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.336
Not only was she wildly
uninformed,

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:15.141
but "60 Minutes" is also
her longest work day so far.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:18.144 line:0%
Also, a side thing,
why fire Tillerson today?

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.646
Well, just yesterday, Tillerson
said the attempted poisoning

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:23.515
of an ex-spy in London "clearly
came from Russia

00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:25.884
and that the incident will
trigger a response."

00:01:25.884 --> 00:01:28.021
Hey, just don't -- He just
didn't know the response

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:30.556
would be, "Clean out your desk."

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:31.824 line:0%
Third thing...

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.259 line:0%
hopefully what we're seeing
with the resignation

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.795
of Gary Cohn and the firing
of Rex Tillerson

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:38.297
is the end
of this myth that serious people

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:39.798
can reign in Donald Trump.

00:01:39.798 --> 00:01:42.535
If the White House is
a fraternity in an '80s movie,

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:46.072
Tillerson was the dean,
and the dean never wins

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.107
in an '80s movie.

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:50.176
"Now, listen up, Delta house,
I'm going out of town

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:53.679
for a business trip, and I don't
want trouble while I'm gone."

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:57.350
"Oh, sure thing, Dean Tillerson.
I promise.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:01.621
I promise we won't do anything
to get you fired."

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.455 line:0%
Final thing, the only thing
more puzzling

00:02:03.455 --> 00:02:05.424 line:0%
than people agreeing to work
for Donald Trump

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:07.060
18 months ago are people

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.662
who are agreeing
to work for him now.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:12.665
I mean, I get the first few
ninjas who thought

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:15.735
they could take down Uma Thurman
in "Kill Bill,"

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:18.137
but what was the last guy
thinking?

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:20.206
"Oh, I get it. If I come at her
from the right.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.241
Also, I'll yell first."

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:23.575
And don't get me wrong.

00:02:23.575 --> 00:02:26.145
I do feel some sympathy
for the Cohns and Tillersons

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:28.414
of this administration,
but in the same way

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.583
I feel sympathy when someone
gets attacked by a gorilla

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.917
at the zoo.

00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:34.319
And that my first thought is,
"Oh, that's horrible."

00:02:34.319 --> 00:02:35.521
And my second thought is,

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:38.825
"Why'd you go into the [bleep]
gorilla cage?"

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:40.260
This has been a "Couple Things."

